sentences.l:
To-her (is) a skin like the silk, and a speech * soft of the edges: no babble and no [scant-word];
and two-eyes to-which God said “Be!”, and they-were, * great-doers to the minds of what the wine does.
So O love-of-her, increase-me in-burning every night, * and O consolation of the lovers, your appointed-time (is) the Gathering.

sentences.i:
Her skin is like silk, and her speech is soft at the edges, neither babbling nor too sparing;
and she has two eyes to which God said “Be!”, and they were, and they work on men's minds as wine does.
O love of her, add to my burning every night; and O comfort of lovers, we shall meet only at the Day of Gathering.

A face that vies in splendour with heaven's lamp, with youth showing on it like a dew of water;
the down upon his cheeks has worked letters into their two fine veils, and folded in those letters lies all the meaning of love.
When I met him, Beauty cried him out like a crier at a sale: “Here is the finely worked piece from God's own embroidery!”
